+If the server reports that this installation authorization was revoked with HTTP 401 or 403 (including
+account deletion), `connect` removes the stale local authorization, pending automatic state, and owned
+hooks through the normal lifecycle cleanup, then starts a fresh pairing without requiring an abandoned
+pairing or changing the installation identity or local source definitions. Partial auxiliary cleanup is
+reported as a warning after the revoked authorization is removed. Other reconciliation errors, including
+transient network failures, leave the existing connection in place and do not start a replacement pairing.
 
